		subs: [
			{ t: 0.00, e: 2.41, en: 'Unit 2. Falling Leaves', vi: '' },
			{ t: 3.52, e: 9.24, en: 'Autumn or fall is the season between summer and winter. The days become shorter and the air gets', vi: '' },
			{ t: 9.54, e: 15.05, en: 'cooler. Trees sense these changes, so they start preparing for colder weather.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 15.90, e: 21.03, en: 'Trees that have leaves block water and food from coming through the branches to the leaves.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 21.42, e: 27.55, en: 'When this happens, the leaves die. They fall off the tree or the wind blows them away.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 28.10, e: 31.79, en: 'This is why autumn is usually called fall in America.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 32.56, e: 39.35, en: 'As the leaves start to die, they appear to change from green to red, yellow, orange or brown.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 40.02, e: 45.94, en: 'Actually, the leaves are really these colors all year long. They look green because of a chemical', vi: '' },
			{ t: 46.24, e: 53.08, en: 'called chlorophyll. Chlorophyll works with the sun to help the trees make food. In autumn, when there', vi: '' },
			{ t: 53.38, e: 59.86, en: 'is less sun, the tree cannot make chlorophyll, so the green color fades. This reveals other colors', vi: '' },
			{ t: 60.16, e: 67.64, en: 'like red and yellow that were always in the leaves. Like trees, animals also sense changes in the', vi: '' },
			{ t: 67.94, e: 73.94, en: 'cooler autumn climate. Animals that hibernate eat a lot during autumn. They gain weight to store', vi: '' },
			{ t: 74.24, e: 80.29, en: 'energy in the form of fat. They use this energy to survive the winter while hibernating.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 81.00, e: 84.93, en: 'Many birds survive the cold in a different way. They leave.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 85.62, e: 89.79, en: 'Each year, many birds migrate south to warmer climates during autumn.', vi: '' },
			{ t: 90.50, e: 96.80, en: 'They migrate north again in the spring. Not a bad idea if you ask me. After all, who would', vi: '' },
			{ t: 97.10, e: 99.71, en: 'refuse a mid-winter trip to sunny Thailand?', vi: '' },
		]
